---
title: "Atomic Tokens: Bridging the Figma-to-Production Chasm"
date: 2024-05-03
readTime: 5 min read
description: "How structured semantic design token architecture completely eliminates drift between design prototypes and frontend components."
tags:
  - Design Systems
  - Engineering
tagColor: sky
---

Every design system eventually confronts the same failure mode: the prototype and the product quietly diverge. A button radius changes in Figma, the code never hears about it, and six months later the "single source of truth" is two sources of truth pointing at each other.

Semantic tokens end the drift. Instead of hardcoding values, both design and code consume the same named decisions — `surface-raised`, `accent-primary`, `radius-control` — resolved from one shared definition file. Change the definition, and Figma variables, the component library, and documentation all move together.

The chasm was never about tooling. It was about naming: teams that agree on vocabulary ship coherence, and teams that don't ship exceptions.
